From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 20:49:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(gateway): a clarify result keeps what its card needs

The stored clarify tool result now carries, per question, multi_select,
answered_at (epoch seconds) and answered_via (the client that answered:
hub, telegram, or the chat platform of a typed reply), and for the call
ended_at and, for a timeout, timeout_s. clarify.settled carries the same
with outcome (answered, skipped, timed_out, cancelled), the question, its
choices, the answer and the subagent that asked, so a viewer can draw a
finished question from stored data after a reload or a restart. Before, the
result held only the question, the choices and the answer, and a client
could show nothing more than "Answered".

clarify.respond takes an optional via (runtime.describe lists
clarify-card-v1). An answer typed in a chat platform records that platform.
